WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.990
The Black Order aka Cull Obsidian, aka the
Children of Thanos are Thanos' trusted gang

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.720
of personal supervillains.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.800
In Avengers: Infinity War, the quartet helps
with Thanos' mission to acquire all six stones

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.080
of the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.349
But in the comics that they come from, the
group goes on all sorts of missions for the

00:00:18.349 --> 00:00:21.329
Mad Titan some of them downright wacky.

00:00:21.329 --> 00:00:25.280
In making the transition to the big screen,
the group had their numbers reduced, their

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.419
members renamed, and their power sets switched
up.

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:32.540
Whether you've already seen Infinity War and
have a few lingering questions, or want a

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.590
quick primer before you check the movie out,
we'll break down everything you need to know

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.629
about Thanos' Black Order.

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:41.519
Cull Obsidian

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:46.839
Introduced by writer Jonathan Hickman in the
2013 Thanos centric storyline Infinity, the

00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:49.179
group originally consisted of five members.

00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:54.899
Thanos' personal starting lineup consists
of Corvus Glaive, Black Dwarf, Proxima Midnight,

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:57.460
Ebony Maw, and Supergiant.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.980
In the Infinity storyline, the Black Order
serve as Thanos' heralds and tax collectors.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:08.110
Their purpose is to roam from world to world,
extracting tributes from planetary populations

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.780
in order to please their master.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.270
The skilled set

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.450
Aside from being pure evil, doggedly loyal,
and aesthetically edgy, what do the Black

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.909
Order have to offer?

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:24.750
Corvus is strong, fast, invulnerable, and
thanks to a magical glaive weapon, conditionally

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.750
immortal.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:31.130
His wife, Proxima Midnight, is similarly powerful
and loyal to Thanos, with a three pronged

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:36.520
spear that when thrown possesses homing capabilities,
fueled by lethal black light.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.869
Black Dwarf was renamed Cull Obsidian for
Infinity War.

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:44.259
His power set, however, remains the same,
since he's the big bruiser of the Black Order

00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:45.259
team.

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:48.680
He's strong, brutish, heavy, and has unbreakable
skin.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.869
Ebony Maw is the brains of the operation,
a physically unimposing telepath who uses

00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:56.330
his sinister wits to divide and conquer.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:01.399
Manipulative and devious, this scrawny brainiac
is typically the member of the team you most

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:03.649
want to see get the Hulk smash treatment.

00:02:03.649 --> 00:02:08.510
These four made it to the Infinity War movie
more or less intact, but they also subsumed

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:13.190
the abilities of the comics' fifth member,
who didn't make the cut.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.190
Supergiant

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:20.480
When the rest of the Black Order made their
big promotional debut at Disney's D23 Expo,

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.980
Supergiant was conspicuously absent.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:28.250
In the Infinity storyline, the blue skinned
Supergiant is an integral member of the team,

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:32.810
an immensely powerful psychic who is able
to control physical matter and also other

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.240
superheroes' minds.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.810
Though she dies in the story that introduces
her, she's so powerful that she was able to

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:42.290
continue existing later on with no physical
body.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:47.500
According to co director Joe Russo, her absence
was mostly necessitated by the movie's already

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.350
obscenely large cast, telling Coming Soon,

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:54.420
"We are dealing with so many characters that
we made some choices along the way.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.890
[...] And frankly, when you see the movie,
you'll understand.

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:00.120
It services the storytelling."

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.400
Corvus takes control

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:06.170
The Black Order's comic history isn't confined
to the Infinity storyline.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:11.930
After that Earth invading crossover event
ends with Thanos and Proxima Midnight in captivity,

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:14.430
Corvus Glaive decides to keep Thanos' throne
warm.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:19.090
With his wife and his master both out of the
picture, Corvus sets up headquarters on a

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:24.200
moon and forms a new version of the Black
Order, a massive army with less specialized

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.200
superpowers than the previous group.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:31.400
It's a pretty good situation for the former
bootlicker until Thanos comes back, and reintroduces

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.010
his boots to Corvus' face.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:38.900
In taking control of Corvus' Black Order,
Thanos decapitates the organization, taking

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.260
out his former second in command within the
first moments of his return.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.840
Thanos doesn't do him in with his own two
hands instead, he forces Corvus to take up

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.080
the shattered pieces of his own weapon and
take his own life.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.100
Brutal.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.150
Hammer time

00:03:55.150 --> 00:04:00.010
After Corvus was dealt with, Thanos formed
a new Black Order, this time with ride or

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:05.450
die OG member Proxima Midnight and the multiversal
traveler Black Swan.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:09.340
This stripped down iteration of the Black
Order was formed for the sake of committing

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:10.340
a heist.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:14.840
This story, told in the pages of The Unworthy
Thor, followed the group's quest to fetch

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.480
an alternate universe version of Thor's hammer,
Mjolnir, for Thanos' use.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.640
"Little Mjolnir, here.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:25.199
Pair of sunglasses in case it gets bright
on the rainbow bridge, which often it does.

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:28.250
If you lift up this little thing, what's he
holding?

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:29.250
Me."

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:33.060
The team was joined by Hela, god of death,
and embarked on a quest to liberate the hammer

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.319
from the Collector.

00:04:34.319 --> 00:04:38.710
Somehow, they didn't succeed, making this
iteration of the Black Order the clearest

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:44.070
sign yet of the team's diminishing returns
as it cycles through new rosters.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.599
No Surrender

00:04:45.599 --> 00:04:51.009
The 2016 Avengers storyline "No Surrender"
reduced the Black Order to their classic roles

00:04:51.009 --> 00:04:53.569
as pawns of a much stronger entity.

00:04:53.569 --> 00:04:58.240
As part of a contest between the Grandmaster
and the Challenger, the Black Order were pitted

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:03.139
against a version of the Lethal Legion to
duke it out in a world spanning scavenger

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:04.139
hunt.

00:05:04.139 --> 00:05:08.330
By the time this storyline rolled around,
many of the Black Order had died, necessitating

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.389
a mass scale revival of the dead members.

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:15.360
This iteration of the team brought the whole
band back together, with the group forced

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:19.800
to go up against not only the Lethal Legion,
but also multiple teams of Avengers.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.999
And they thought working for Thanos was bad.

00:05:22.999 --> 00:05:24.599
Blockbuster night

00:05:24.599 --> 00:05:29.030
Principally identified as the Children of
Thanos, the Black Order showed up in Avengers:

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:33.380
Infinity War to cause trouble for the heroes
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:37.340
The movie sees Corvus Glaive portrayed by
actor Michael Shaw, Proxima Midnight played

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:42.389
by The Leftovers' Carrie Coon, Irish actor
Tom Vaughan Lawlor taking on the role of Ebony

00:05:42.389 --> 00:05:48.039
Maw, and stunt performer Terry Notary as the
renamed Black Dwarf, Cull Obsidian.

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:52.409
It's a good thing Nebula and Gamora's family
issues got in the way of their being on Thanos'

00:05:52.409 --> 00:05:53.409
team for this fight.

00:05:53.409 --> 00:05:54.780
With their help, who knows?

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.889
The Black Order might have been pretty much
unstoppable.

00:05:57.889 --> 00:05:58.919
Thanks for watching!

00:05:58.919 --> 00:06:01.789
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:01.789 --> 00:06:04.310
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

